IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`
IMPORT `pip-part1-general`
IMPORT `pip-part4-residence`

-- PART 4 -- RESIDENCE AND PRESENCE CONDITIONS, second half: regulations 22 to 23A, and the combination of
-- regulation 16 with every regulation that modifies it.
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Regulations 22, 23 and 23A disapply limbs of regulation 16; regulation 23ZA
-- treats limb (c) as not satisfied; regulations 23ZB and 23ZC treat C as present in England and Wales for a
-- run-on period after a move to Scotland and extend a fixed-term award. The text does not say what happens when
-- regulation 23ZA meets a regulation that disapplies or deems limb (c) satisfied (fork F-22); the combining rule
-- at the end answers "the text does not say" for that case.

§ `Regulation 22: persons residing in Great Britain to whom a relevant EU Regulation applies`

-- reg 22: regulation 16(b) does not apply in relation to a claim for personal independence payment where on any day
-- (a) C is habitually resident in Great Britain; (b) a relevant EU Regulation applies; and (c) C can demonstrate a
-- genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom. (The converter's "..." marks words omitted from the text.)
-- out of text: what a "relevant EU Regulation" is; the reading of "genuine and sufficient link" is a fact C states
-- src:243 | 22 Persons residing in Great Britain to whom a relevant EU Regulation applies
-- src:244 | Regulation 16(b) does not apply in relation to a claim for personal independence payment where on any day–
-- src:245 | (a) C is habitually resident in Great Britain;
-- src:246 | (b) a relevant EU Regulation applies; and
-- src:247 | (c) C can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom ... .
@ref reg 22 (src:244-247)
GIVEN `C is habitually resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a relevant EU Regulation applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22: regulation 16(b) does not apply on the day` MEANS
        `C is habitually resident in Great Britain`
    AND `a relevant EU Regulation applies`
    AND `C can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom`

§ `Regulation 23: persons residing in an EEA state or in Switzerland to whom a relevant EU Regulation applies`

-- The date 31 December 2020, named in regulation 23(b)(ii).
-- src:255 | (ii) except where C has been habitually resident in the United Kingdom after 31st December 2020, applied to C on 31st December 2020 and they have been continuously in receipt of the daily living component of personal independence payment on and from that date; and
@ref reg 23(b)(ii) (src:255)
`the day 31st December 2020` MEANS YearMonthDay 2020 12 31

-- reg 23(a): C is habitually resident in (i) an EEA state; or (ii) Switzerland. The Republic of Ireland is an EEA state.
-- src:250 | (a) C is habitually resident in–
-- src:251 | (i) an EEA state ...; or
-- src:252 | (ii) Switzerland;
@ref reg 23(a) (src:250-252)
GIVEN place IS A `a place of habitual residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23(a): C is habitually resident in an EEA state or Switzerland` place MEANS
       place EQUALS `the Republic of Ireland`
    OR place EQUALS `an EEA state other than the Republic of Ireland`
    OR place EQUALS `Switzerland`

-- reg 23(b): a relevant EU Regulation (i) applies to C; or (ii) except where C has been habitually resident in the
-- United Kingdom after 31st December 2020, applied to C on 31st December 2020 and they have been continuously in
-- receipt of the daily living component of personal independence payment on and from that date.
-- The first limb reads the exception as: C has not been habitually resident in the United Kingdom on any day after
-- 31 December 2020, and "continuously in receipt on and from that date" as: C's continuous receipt began on or
-- before 31 December 2020 (and runs to the day).
-- src:253 | (b) a relevant EU Regulation—
-- src:254 | (i) applies to C; or
-- src:255 | (ii) except where C has been habitually resident in the United Kingdom after 31st December 2020, applied to C on 31st December 2020 and they have been continuously in receipt of the daily living component of personal independence payment on and from that date; and
@ref reg 23(b) (src:253-255)
GIVEN `a relevant EU Regulation applies to C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a relevant EU Regulation applied to C on 31 December 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the latest day on which C has been habitually resident in the United Kingdom` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the first day of C's continuous receipt of the daily living component, running to the day` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23(b): a relevant EU Regulation applies to C, or applied to C on 31 December 2020 and C has been in continuous receipt` MEANS
       `a relevant EU Regulation applies to C`
    OR `reg 23(b)(ii): the second limb is met`
           `a relevant EU Regulation applied to C on 31 December 2020`
           `the latest day on which C has been habitually resident in the United Kingdom`
           `the first day of C's continuous receipt of the daily living component, running to the day`

@ref reg 23(b)(ii) (src:255)
GIVEN `a relevant EU Regulation applied to C on 31 December 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the latest day on which C has been habitually resident in the United Kingdom` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the first day of C's continuous receipt of the daily living component, running to the day` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23(b)(ii): the second limb is met` MEANS
        `a relevant EU Regulation applied to C on 31 December 2020`
    AND (NOT `reg 23(b)(ii): C has been habitually resident in the United Kingdom after 31 December 2020` `the latest day on which C has been habitually resident in the United Kingdom`)
    AND `reg 23(b)(ii): C has been continuously in receipt on and from 31 December 2020` `the first day of C's continuous receipt of the daily living component, running to the day`

@ref reg 23(b)(ii) (src:255)
GIVEN latest IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23(b)(ii): C has been habitually resident in the United Kingdom after 31 December 2020` latest MEANS
    CONSIDER latest
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d THEN d GREATER THAN `the day 31st December 2020`

@ref reg 23(b)(ii) (src:255)
GIVEN first IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23(b)(ii): C has been continuously in receipt on and from 31 December 2020` first MEANS
    CONSIDER first
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d THEN d AT MOST `the day 31st December 2020`

-- reg 23: regulation 16(a) to (c) does not apply in relation to entitlement to the daily living component of personal
-- independence payment where on any day (a), (b) and (c) (C can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom).
-- Regulation 16(d) is not mentioned and so still applies. The disapplication is for the daily living component only; the
-- combining rule at the end applies it to that component.
-- src:248 | 23 Persons residing in an EEA state ... or in Switzerland to whom a relevant EU Regulation applies
-- src:249 | Regulation 16(a) to (c) does not apply in relation to entitlement to the daily living component of personal independence payment where on any day—
-- src:256 | (c) C can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom ... .
@ref reg 23 (src:249, src:256)
GIVEN `C is habitually resident in an EEA state or Switzerland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a relevant EU Regulation applies to C, or applied to C on 31 December 2020 and C has been in continuous receipt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23: regulation 16(a) to (c) do not apply to the daily living component on the day` MEANS
        `C is habitually resident in an EEA state or Switzerland`
    AND `a relevant EU Regulation applies to C, or applied to C on 31 December 2020 and C has been in continuous receipt`
    AND `C can demonstrate a genuine and sufficient link to the United Kingdom`

§ `Regulation 23ZA: persons in receipt of an equivalent Scottish benefit who move from Scotland to England or Wales`

-- reg 23ZA(1): where regulation 36(1) of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations
-- 2021 applies to C, regulation 16(c) of these Regulations is treated as not satisfied for the period set out in
-- regulation 36(1) of those Regulations.
-- out of text: Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 reg 36(1)
-- src:257 | 23ZA Persons in receipt of an equivalent Scottish benefit who move from Scotland to England or Wales
-- src:258 | (1) Where regulation 36(1) of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 applies to C, regulation 16(c) of these Regulations is treated as not satisfied for the period set out in regulation 36(1) of those Regulations.
@ref reg 23ZA(1) (src:258)
GIVEN `regulation 36(1) of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 applies to C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day is within the period set out in regulation 36(1) of those Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZA(1): regulation 16(c) is treated as not satisfied on the day` MEANS
        `regulation 36(1) of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021 applies to C`
    AND `the day is within the period set out in regulation 36(1) of those Regulations`

-- reg 23ZA(2): the same where regulation 53(1) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland)
-- Regulations 2022 applies to C.
-- out of text: Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 reg 53(1)
-- src:259 | (2) Where regulation 53(1) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 applies to C, regulation 16(c) of these Regulations is treated as not satisfied for the period set out in regulation 53(1) of those Regulations.
@ref reg 23ZA(2) (src:259)
GIVEN `regulation 53(1) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 applies to C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day is within the period set out in regulation 53(1) of those Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZA(2): regulation 16(c) is treated as not satisfied on the day` MEANS
        `regulation 53(1) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 applies to C`
    AND `the day is within the period set out in regulation 53(1) of those Regulations`

@ref reg 23ZA(1), reg 23ZA(2) (src:258, src:259)
GIVEN `paragraph (1) treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZA: regulation 16(c) is treated as not satisfied on the day by paragraph (1) or (2)` MEANS
       `paragraph (1) treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied on the day`
    OR `paragraph (2) treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied on the day`

§ `Regulation 23ZB: effect of move to Scotland (C entitled to personal independence payment)`

-- The date 6 November 2025, named in regulations 23ZB(1) and 23ZC(2)(b) and (4).
-- src:261 | (1) This regulation applies where C becomes permanently resident in Scotland on or after 6th November 2025.
-- src:274 | (b) becomes permanently resident in Scotland on or after 6th November 2025, and
-- src:282 | (4) Where the day referred to in paragraph (i) or (ii) of paragraph (2)(c) is before 6th November 2025, the condition in that paragraph is to be read to the effect that the person must be present in England and Wales, or treated for the purposes of regulation 16(a) as being present in Great Britain, on that day.
@ref reg 23ZB(1), reg 23ZC(2)(b), reg 23ZC(4) (src:261, src:274, src:282)
`the day 6th November 2025` MEANS YearMonthDay 2025 11 6

-- reg 23ZB(1): this regulation applies where C becomes permanently resident in Scotland on or after 6th November 2025.
-- src:260 | 23ZB Effect of move to Scotland (C entitled to personal independence payment)
-- src:261 | (1) This regulation applies where C becomes permanently resident in Scotland on or after 6th November 2025.
@ref reg 23ZB(1) (src:261)
GIVEN `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZB(1): this regulation applies` MEANS
    (`reg 2: the residence change date` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`) AT LEAST `the day 6th November 2025`

-- reg 23ZB(4): "the run-on period", in relation to a person, is the period (a) beginning with the residence change
-- date, and (b) ending at the end of the period of 13 weeks beginning on the residence change date.
-- src:267 | (4) “The run-on period”, in relation to a person, is the period—
-- src:268 | (a) beginning with the residence change date, and
-- src:269 | (b) ending at the end of the period of 13 weeks beginning on the residence change date.
@ref reg 23ZB(4) (src:267-269)
GIVEN `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 23ZB(4): the first day of the run-on period` MEANS
    `reg 2: the residence change date` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`

@ref reg 23ZB(4) (src:267-269)
GIVEN `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 23ZB(4): the last day of the run-on period` MEANS
    `the last day of the weeks beginning with` (`reg 2: the residence change date` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`) `for` 13

-- A day is in the run-on period if it is on or after its first day and on or before its last.
@ref reg 23ZB(4) (src:267-269)
GIVEN `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZB(4): the day is in the run-on period` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` `on` `the day` MEANS
        `the day` AT LEAST (`reg 23ZB(4): the first day of the run-on period` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`)
    AND `the day` AT MOST (`reg 23ZB(4): the last day of the run-on period` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`)

-- reg 23ZB(2): if, on the day before the residence change date, C is entitled to any component of personal independence
-- payment, C is, insofar as they are not present in England and Wales on or after the residence change date, to be treated
-- as present in England and Wales for the purposes of regulation 16(a) for the duration of the run-on period.
-- src:262 | (2) If, on the day before the residence change date, C is entitled to any component of personal independence payment, C is, insofar as they are not present in England and Wales on or after the residence change date, to be treated as present in England and Wales for the purposes of regulation 16(a) for the duration of the run-on period.
@ref reg 23ZB(2) (src:262)
GIVEN `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
      `C is entitled to a component of personal independence payment on the day before the residence change date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZB(2): C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` `with` `C is entitled to a component of personal independence payment on the day before the residence change date` `on` `the day` MEANS
        `reg 23ZB(1): this regulation applies` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`
    AND `C is entitled to a component of personal independence payment on the day before the residence change date`
    AND `reg 23ZB(4): the day is in the run-on period` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` `on` `the day`

-- reg 23ZB(3): if, on the day before the residence change date, (a) C has an award of any component which is for a fixed
-- term period, and (b) that fixed term period is due to expire before the end of the run-on period, the fixed term period
-- is extended so that it expires at the same time as the run-on period. A period due to expire on the last day of the
-- run-on period is not due to expire before the end of it.
-- src:263 | (3) If, on the day before the residence change date—
-- src:264 | (a) C has an award of any component of personal independence payment which is for a fixed term period, and
-- src:265 | (b) that fixed term period is due to expire before the end of the run-on period,
-- src:266 | the fixed term period is extended so that it expires at the same time as the run-on period.
@ref reg 23ZB(3) (src:263-266)
GIVEN `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
      `C has an award of a component for a fixed term period on the day before the residence change date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the fixed term period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 23ZB(3): the last day of the fixed term period after any extension` MEANS
    IF     `reg 23ZB(1): this regulation applies` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`
       AND `C has an award of a component for a fixed term period on the day before the residence change date`
       AND `the last day of the fixed term period` LESS THAN (`reg 23ZB(4): the last day of the run-on period` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`)
    THEN `reg 23ZB(4): the last day of the run-on period` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`
    ELSE `the last day of the fixed term period`

§ `Regulation 23ZC: effect of move to Scotland (ongoing claim)`

-- reg 23ZC(3): for the purposes of paragraph (2)(a), C has an ongoing claim on the residence change date if, before that
-- date, the claim has not (a) been decided by the Secretary of State under section 8 of the 1998 Act, (b) been withdrawn
-- in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments Regulations, or (c) otherwise ceased to be under consideration
-- before being decided by the Secretary of State under section 8 of the 1998 Act.
-- out of text: Social Security Act 1998 s 8; Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Claims and Payments) Regulations 2013 reg 31
-- src:278 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(a), C has an ongoing claim on the residence change date if, before that date, the claim has not—
-- src:279 | (a) been decided by the Secretary of State under section 8 of the 1998 Act,
-- src:280 | (b) been withdrawn in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments Regulations, or
-- src:281 | (c) otherwise ceased to be under consideration before being decided by the Secretary of State under section 8 of the 1998 Act.
@ref reg 23ZC(3) (src:278-281)
GIVEN `the claim was decided by the Secretary of State under section 8 of the 1998 Act before the residence change date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim was withdrawn in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments Regulations before the residence change date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim otherwise ceased to be under consideration before being decided by the Secretary of State before the residence change date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZC(3): C has an ongoing claim on the residence change date` MEANS
        (NOT `the claim was decided by the Secretary of State under section 8 of the 1998 Act before the residence change date`)
    AND (NOT `the claim was withdrawn in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments Regulations before the residence change date`)
    AND (NOT `the claim otherwise ceased to be under consideration before being decided by the Secretary of State before the residence change date`)

-- reg 23ZC(2)(c), with (4): C is, or in accordance with a provision other than this regulation is treated for the purposes of
-- regulation 16(a) as being, present in England and Wales on a day. Where the day is before 6 November 2025 the condition
-- is read as: C must be present in England and Wales, or treated for the purposes of regulation 16(a) as being present in
-- Great Britain, on that day.
-- src:275 | (c) is, or in accordance with a provision other than this regulation is treated for the purposes of regulation 16(a) as being, present in England and Wales—
-- src:276 | (i) on the day on which C makes the claim, and
-- src:277 | (ii) on the day before the residence change date.
-- src:282 | (4) Where the day referred to in paragraph (i) or (ii) of paragraph (2)(c) is before 6th November 2025, the condition in that paragraph is to be read to the effect that the person must be present in England and Wales, or treated for the purposes of regulation 16(a) as being present in Great Britain, on that day.
@ref reg 23ZC(2)(c), reg 23ZC(4) (src:275-277, src:282)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `C is present in England and Wales on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is treated, in accordance with a provision other than regulation 23ZC, as present in England and Wales for the purposes of regulation 16(a) on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is treated for the purposes of regulation 16(a) as present in Great Britain on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZC(2)(c) and (4): C is present or treated as present on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` LESS THAN `the day 6th November 2025`
    THEN `C is present in England and Wales on the day` OR `C is treated for the purposes of regulation 16(a) as present in Great Britain on the day`
    ELSE `C is present in England and Wales on the day` OR `C is treated, in accordance with a provision other than regulation 23ZC, as present in England and Wales for the purposes of regulation 16(a) on the day`

-- reg 23ZC(1) and (2): where C satisfies the conditions in paragraph (2) -- that C (a) has an ongoing claim on the
-- residence change date, (b) becomes permanently resident in Scotland on or after 6th November 2025, and (c) is, or is
-- treated as, present in England and Wales (i) on the day on which C makes the claim and (ii) on the day before the
-- residence change date -- the Secretary of State must comply with the requirement in paragraph (5).
-- src:271 | (1) Where C satisfies the conditions in paragraph (2), the Secretary of State must comply with the requirement in paragraph (5).
-- src:272 | (2) The conditions mentioned in paragraph (1) are, subject to paragraph (4), that C—
-- src:273 | (a) has an ongoing claim for personal independence payment on the residence change date,
-- src:274 | (b) becomes permanently resident in Scotland on or after 6th November 2025, and
-- src:275 | (c) is, or in accordance with a provision other than this regulation is treated for the purposes of regulation 16(a) as being, present in England and Wales—
-- src:276 | (i) on the day on which C makes the claim, and
-- src:277 | (ii) on the day before the residence change date.
@ref reg 23ZC(1), reg 23ZC(2) (src:271-277)
GIVEN `C has an ongoing claim on the residence change date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
      `C is present or treated as present on the day on which C makes the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is present or treated as present on the day before the residence change date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZC(2): C satisfies the conditions` MEANS
        `C has an ongoing claim on the residence change date`
    AND (`reg 2: the residence change date` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`) AT LEAST `the day 6th November 2025`
    AND `C is present or treated as present on the day on which C makes the claim`
    AND `C is present or treated as present on the day before the residence change date`

-- reg 23ZC(5): the Secretary of State must make a decision under section 8 of the 1998 Act on C's claim for personal
-- independence payment, unless C withdraws the claim in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments
-- Regulations. A duty of the Secretary of State; C's right to a decision.
-- src:283 | (5) The requirement mentioned in paragraph (1) is that the Secretary of State must make a decision under section 8 of the 1998 Act on C’s claim for personal independence payment, unless C withdraws the claim in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments Regulations.
@ref reg 23ZC(5) (src:283)
GIVEN `C satisfies the conditions in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C withdraws the claim in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZC(1) and (5): the Secretary of State must decide C's claim under section 8 of the 1998 Act` MEANS
        `C satisfies the conditions in paragraph (2)`
    AND (NOT `C withdraws the claim in accordance with regulation 31 of the Claims and Payments Regulations`)

-- reg 23ZC(6): for the purposes of the decision mentioned in paragraph (5), regulation 16(a) applies as if for
-- "England and Wales" there were substituted "Great Britain".
-- src:284 | (6) For the purposes of the decision of the Secretary of State mentioned in paragraph (5), regulation 16(a) applies as if for “England and Wales” there were substituted “Great Britain”.
@ref reg 23ZC(6) (src:284)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State must decide C's claim under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZC(6): regulation 16(a) is read with "Great Britain" in place of "England and Wales" for the decision` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State must decide C's claim under paragraph (5)`

-- reg 23ZC(7)(a): if the Secretary of State decides that C is entitled to any component, C is, insofar as they are not
-- present in England and Wales on or after the residence change date, to be treated as present in England and Wales for
-- the purposes of regulation 16(a) for the duration of the run-on period.
-- src:285 | (7) If the Secretary of State decides that C is entitled to any component of personal independence payment—
-- src:286 | (a) C is, insofar as they are not present in England and Wales on or after the residence change date, to be treated as present in England and Wales for the purposes of regulation 16(a) for the duration of the run-on period, and
@ref reg 23ZC(7)(a) (src:285-286)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State must decide C's claim under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State decides that C is entitled to a component of personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23ZC(7)(a): C is treated as present in England and Wales on the day` MEANS
        `the Secretary of State must decide C's claim under paragraph (5)`
    AND `the Secretary of State decides that C is entitled to a component of personal independence payment`
    AND `reg 23ZB(4): the day is in the run-on period` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` `on` `the day`

-- reg 23ZC(7)(b): if (i) C has an award of any component which is for a fixed term period, and (ii) the fixed term
-- period is due to expire before the end of the run-on period, the fixed term period is extended so that it expires at
-- the same time as the run-on period.
-- src:287 | (b) if—
-- src:288 | (i) C has an award of any component of personal independence payment which is for a fixed term period, and
-- src:289 | (ii) the fixed term period is due to expire before the end of the run-on period,
-- src:290 | the fixed term period is extended so that it expires at the same time as the run-on period.
@ref reg 23ZC(7)(b) (src:287-290)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State must decide C's claim under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State decides that C is entitled to a component of personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland` IS A DATE
      `C has an award of a component for a fixed term period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the fixed term period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 23ZC(7)(b): the last day of the fixed term period after any extension` MEANS
    IF     `the Secretary of State must decide C's claim under paragraph (5)`
       AND `the Secretary of State decides that C is entitled to a component of personal independence payment`
       AND `C has an award of a component for a fixed term period`
       AND `the last day of the fixed term period` LESS THAN (`reg 23ZB(4): the last day of the run-on period` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`)
    THEN `reg 23ZB(4): the last day of the run-on period` `the date on which C becomes permanently resident in Scotland`
    ELSE `the last day of the fixed term period`

-- reg 23ZC(8): (a) "the Claims and Payments Regulations" means the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment,
-- Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Claims and Payments) Regulations 2013; (b) any reference to
-- the date on which a person makes a claim for personal independence payment (however expressed) is to be construed in
-- accordance with regulation 12 of those Regulations. Both are definitions of terms used by inputs above.
-- src:291 | (8) In this regulation—
-- src:292 | (a) the “Claims and Payments Regulations” means the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker’s Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Claims and Payments) Regulations 2013;
-- src:293 | (b) any reference to the date on which a person makes a claim for personal independence payment (however expressed) is to be construed in accordance with regulation 12 of the Claims and Payments Regulations.
@ref reg 23ZC(8) (src:291-293)
`reg 23ZC(8): definitions` MEANS
    "(8) In this regulation (a) the \"Claims and Payments Regulations\" means the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Claims and Payments) Regulations 2013; (b) the date on which a person makes a claim is to be construed in accordance with regulation 12 of those Regulations."

§ `Regulation 23A: refugees and certain persons with leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom`

-- reg 23A(2): for the purposes of this regulation (a) "immigration rules" means the rules laid before Parliament under
-- section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971; (b) "the Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme" means the scheme announced by
-- the United Kingdom Government on 18 August 2021. Both are definitions of terms used by inputs below; the date identifies
-- the scheme and no rule tests anything against it. The converter shows the same sentence for "immigration rules" as a
-- repealed paragraph (2) (src:347), read as struck.
-- src:348 | (2) For the purposes of this regulation—
-- src:349 | (a) “immigration rules” means the rules laid before Parliament under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971,
-- src:350 | (b) “the Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme” means the scheme announced by the United Kingdom Government on 18 August 2021.
@ref reg 23A(2) (src:348-350)
`reg 23A(2): definitions` MEANS
    "(2) For the purposes of this regulation (a) \"immigration rules\" means the rules laid before Parliament under section 3(2) of the Immigration Act 1971; (b) \"the Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme\" means the scheme announced by the United Kingdom Government on 18 August 2021."

-- reg 23A(1)(c): leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under the immigration rules by virtue of (i) the
-- Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy, or (ii) the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan.
-- src:298 | (c) leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under the immigration rules by virtue of—
-- src:299 | (i) the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy, or
-- src:300 | (ii) the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan (sometimes referred to as the ex-gratia scheme),
@ref reg 23A(1)(c) (src:298-300)
GIVEN `C has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under the immigration rules by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under the immigration rules by virtue of the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23A(1)(c): C has leave granted by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy or the previous scheme` MEANS
       `C has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under the immigration rules by virtue of the Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy`
    OR `C has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under the immigration rules by virtue of the previous scheme for locally-employed staff in Afghanistan`

-- reg 23A(1)(f), (g), (h): leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under or outside the immigration rules,
-- a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971 or does not
-- require leave to enter or remain in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act. The three paragraphs open with the same words.
-- src:303 | (f) leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under or outside the immigration rules , a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971 or does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act, where C—
-- src:306 | (g) leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under or outside the immigration rules, a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971 or does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act, where C—
-- src:309 | (h) leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under or outside the immigration rules, a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971 or does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act, where C—
@ref reg 23A(1)(f), reg 23A(1)(g), reg 23A(1)(h) (src:303, src:306, src:309)
GIVEN `C has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under or outside the immigration rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23A(1)(f), (g), (h): C has leave, a right of abode, or needs no leave` MEANS
       `C has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under or outside the immigration rules`
    OR `C has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971`
    OR `C does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act`

-- reg 23A(1)(f): ... where C (i) was residing in Ukraine immediately before 1 January 2022; and (ii) left Ukraine in
-- connection with the Russian invasion which took place on 24 February 2022.
-- The converter shows "24February 2022" and a repealed ". . ."; the quotation is mechanical.
-- src:303 | (f) leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom granted under or outside the immigration rules , a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971 or does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act, where C—
