    AND `C left Israel, the West Bank, the Gaza Strip, East Jerusalem, the Golan Heights or Lebanon in connection with the Hamas terrorist attack in Israel on 7 October 2023 or the violence which rapidly escalated in the region following the attack`

-- reg 23A(1)(i), conditions A to D (first version, src:312-326): the person met conditions A to D.
-- Condition A: the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's
-- Government (a) provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it, or (b) arranged their evacuation.
-- src:312 | (i) met conditions A to D.
-- src:313 | Condition A
-- src:314 | The person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty’s Government—
-- src:315 | (a) provided public information to advise British nationals to leave that country or territory, or
-- src:316 | (b) arranged the evacuation of British nationals from that country or territory.
@ref reg 23A(1)(i) Condition A (src:313-316)
GIVEN `the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23A(1)(i) Condition A: the person was residing in the country or territory when the advice was given or the evacuation arranged` MEANS
       `the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government provided public information to advise British nationals to leave it`
    OR `the person was residing in a country or territory outside Great Britain immediately before His Majesty's Government arranged the evacuation of British nationals from it`

-- Condition B: the person has left that country or territory.
-- src:317 | Condition B
-- src:318 | The person has left that country or territory.
@ref reg 23A(1)(i) Condition B (src:317-318)
GIVEN `the person has left that country or territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23A(1)(i) Condition B: the person has left the country or territory` MEANS
    `the person has left that country or territory`

-- Condition C: the person arrived in Great Britain in the first 26 weeks beginning on the day on which the public
-- information is issued, or the evacuation is started.
-- src:319 | Condition C
-- src:320 | The person arrived in Great Britain in the first 26 weeks beginning on the day on which the public information is issued, or the evacuation is started.
@ref reg 23A(1)(i) Condition C (src:319-320)
GIVEN `the day the public information was issued or the evacuation was started` IS A DATE
      `the day the person arrived in Great Britain` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23A(1)(i) Condition C: the person arrived in Great Britain in the first 26 weeks` MEANS
        `the day the person arrived in Great Britain` AT LEAST `the day the public information was issued or the evacuation was started`
    AND `the day the person arrived in Great Britain` AT MOST (`the last day of the weeks beginning with` `the day the public information was issued or the evacuation was started` `for` 26)

-- Condition D: the person (a) has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the
-- Immigration Act 1971, (b) does not require leave to enter or remain in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act, (c) has
-- leave to enter or remain in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act, or (d) has leave on
-- a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of that Act.
-- src:321 | Condition D
-- src:322 | The person—
-- src:323 | (a) has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971,
-- src:324 | (b) does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act,
-- src:325 | (c) has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act, or
-- src:326 | (d) has leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of that Act; or
@ref reg 23A(1)(i) Condition D (src:321-326)
GIVEN `the person has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23A(1)(i) Condition D: the person has the right of abode, needs no leave, or has leave` MEANS
       `the person has a right of abode in the United Kingdom within the meaning given in section 2 of the Immigration Act 1971`
    OR `the person does not require leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with section 3ZA of that Act`
    OR `the person has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom in accordance with immigration rules made under section 3(2) of that Act`
    OR `the person has leave on a discretionary basis outside of rules made under section 3(2) of that Act`

@ref reg 23A(1)(i) (src:312)
GIVEN `condition A is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition B is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition C is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition D is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
