    AND `the day` AT MOST (`the last day of the weeks beginning with` `the day the public information was issued or the evacuation was started` `for` 130)

-- reg 23A(1): regulation 16(b) does not apply in relation to a claim for personal independence payment where C has any of
-- (a) to (l); and reg 23A(1A): regulation 16(c) does not apply where any sub-paragraph in paragraph (1) applies to C.
-- (a) refugee status or humanitarian protection; (b) leave as the dependant of such a person; (d) discretionary leave
-- outside the immigration rules as a dependant of a person referred to in (c); (e) leave under the Afghan Citizens
-- Resettlement Scheme: each is a fact C states.
-- src:295 | (1) Regulation 16(b) does not apply in relation to a claim for personal independence payment where C has—
-- src:296 | (a) been granted refugee status or humanitarian protection under the immigration rules; ...
-- src:297 | (b) leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom as the dependant of a person granted refugee status or humanitarian protection under the immigration rules.
-- src:301 | (d) been granted discretionary leave outside the immigration rules as a dependant of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (c); {repealed: ...}
-- src:302 | (e) leave granted under the Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme ; ...
-- src:344 | (1A) Regulation 16(c) does not apply in relation to a claim for personal independence payment where any sub-paragraph in paragraph (1) applies to C.
@ref reg 23A(1), reg 23A(1A) (src:295-297, src:301-302, src:344)
GIVEN `C has been granted refugee status or humanitarian protection under the immigration rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom as the dependant of a person granted refugee status or humanitarian protection under the immigration rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(c) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has been granted discretionary leave outside the immigration rules as a dependant of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has leave granted under the Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(f) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(g) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(h) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(i) applies on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(j) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(k) applies on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (1)(l) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23A(1): a sub-paragraph of paragraph (1) applies to C on the day` MEANS
       `C has been granted refugee status or humanitarian protection under the immigration rules`
    OR `C has leave to enter or remain in the United Kingdom as the dependant of a person granted refugee status or humanitarian protection under the immigration rules`
    OR `paragraph (1)(c) applies`
    OR `C has been granted discretionary leave outside the immigration rules as a dependant of a person referred to in sub-paragraph (c)`
    OR `C has leave granted under the Afghan Citizens Resettlement Scheme`
    OR `paragraph (1)(f) applies`
    OR `paragraph (1)(g) applies`
    OR `paragraph (1)(h) applies`
    OR `paragraph (1)(i) applies on the day`
    OR `paragraph (1)(j) applies`
    OR `paragraph (1)(k) applies on the day`
    OR `paragraph (1)(l) applies`

§ `Regulation 16 with the regulations that modify it`

DECLARE `the outcome of regulation 16 on the day` IS ONE OF
    `the conditions of regulation 16 are met`
    `the conditions of regulation 16 are not met`
    `the text does not say whether the conditions of regulation 16 are met`

-- Limb (a) after regulation 23: regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) for the daily living component.
@ref reg 16(a), reg 23 (src:171, src:249)
GIVEN c IS A `a component of personal independence payment`
      `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 16(a) is met on its own terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(a) as modified: limb (a) is met` c `with` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` `and` `regulation 16(a) is met on its own terms` MEANS
    IF c EQUALS `the daily living component` AND `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `regulation 16(a) is met on its own terms`

-- Limb (b) after regulations 21, 22, 23 and 23A(1): any one of them disapplies it (regulation 23 only for the daily living
-- component). (Regulations 16(b) and 21 are quoted in pip-part4-residence; the locators below are the lines quoted here.)
@ref reg 16(b), reg 21, reg 22, reg 23, reg 23A(1) (src:244, src:249, src:295)
GIVEN c IS A `a component of personal independence payment`
      `regulation 21 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 22 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 23A(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 16(b) is met on its own terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(b) as modified: limb (b) is met` c `with` `regulation 21 applies` `and` `regulation 22 applies` `and` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` `and` `regulation 23A(1) applies` `and` `regulation 16(b) is met on its own terms` MEANS
    IF     `regulation 21 applies`
        OR `regulation 22 applies`
        OR `regulation 23A(1) applies`
        OR (c EQUALS `the daily living component` AND `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `regulation 16(b) is met on its own terms`

-- Limb (c) after regulations 20, 23, 23A(1A) and 23ZA. Regulation 20 treats C as habitually resident in Great Britain; regulations
-- 23 and 23A(1A) say limb (c) does not apply; regulation 23ZA treats limb (c) as not satisfied. When 23ZA meets one of the
-- others the text does not say which prevails (fork F-22): NOTHING. (Regulations 16(c) and 20 are quoted in pip-part4-residence; the
-- locators below are the lines quoted here.)
@ref reg 16(c), reg 20, reg 23, reg 23ZA, reg 23A(1A) (src:249, src:258, src:344)
GIVEN c IS A `a component of personal independence payment`
      `regulation 20 treats C as habitually resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 23A(1A) disapplies regulation 16(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 23ZA treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 16(c) is met on its own terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 16(c) as modified: limb (c) is met` c `with` `regulation 20 treats C as habitually resident in Great Britain` `and` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` `and` `regulation 23A(1A) disapplies regulation 16(c)` `and` `regulation 23ZA treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied` `and` `regulation 16(c) is met on its own terms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `regulation 23ZA treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied` AND `reg 16(c) is deemed or disapplied by another regulation` c `with` `regulation 20 treats C as habitually resident in Great Britain` `and` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` `and` `regulation 23A(1A) disapplies regulation 16(c)`
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `regulation 23ZA treats regulation 16(c) as not satisfied`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `reg 16(c) is deemed or disapplied by another regulation` c `with` `regulation 20 treats C as habitually resident in Great Britain` `and` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` `and` `regulation 23A(1A) disapplies regulation 16(c)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST `regulation 16(c) is met on its own terms`

GIVEN c IS A `a component of personal independence payment`
      `regulation 20 treats C as habitually resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation 23A(1A) disapplies regulation 16(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 16(c) is deemed or disapplied by another regulation` c `with` `regulation 20 treats C as habitually resident in Great Britain` `and` `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)` `and` `regulation 23A(1A) disapplies regulation 16(c)` MEANS
       `regulation 20 treats C as habitually resident in Great Britain`
    OR `regulation 23A(1A) disapplies regulation 16(c)`
    OR (c EQUALS `the daily living component` AND `regulation 23 disapplies regulation 16(a) to (c)`)

-- reg 16 as a whole: all four limbs on the day. Limb (d) is not modified by any later regulation. A limb that is not
-- met makes the conditions not met even if limb (c) is not covered.
-- src:170 | 16 Conditions relating to residence and presence in Great Britain
-- src:171 | Subject to the following provisions of this Part, the prescribed conditions for the purposes of section 77(3) of the Act as to residence and presence in Great Britain are that on any day for which C claims personal independence payment C—
@ref reg 16 (src:171)
GIVEN `limb (a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (c) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `the outcome of regulation 16 on the day`
`reg 16: the outcome on the day` `limb (a) is met` `limb (b) is met` `limb (c) is met` `limb (d) is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `limb (a) is met`) OR (NOT `limb (b) is met`) OR (NOT `limb (d) is met`) THEN `the conditions of regulation 16 are not met`
        IF `limb (c) is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN `the conditions of regulation 16 are not met`
        IF `limb (c) is met` EQUALS NOTHING THEN `the text does not say whether the conditions of regulation 16 are met`
        OTHERWISE `the conditions of regulation 16 are met`
